{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SpicyBadran/PC5/pulls/39","id":5434821191,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVrsYR88AAAABQ_DKRw","html_url":"https://github.com/SpicyBadran/PC5/pull/39","diff_url":"https://github.com/SpicyBadran/PC5/pull/39.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/SpicyBadran/PC5/pull/39.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SpicyBadran/PC5/issues/39","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SpicyBadran/PC5/pulls/39/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SpicyBadran/PC5/pulls/39/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SpicyBadran/PC5/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SpicyBadran/PC5/issues/39/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SpicyBadran/PC5/statuses/003bbdcdef29bdeada06b029828487caa8f6b058","number":39,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"docs(evidence): M18 synthetic-package acceptance item — design assessment (no code: not yet separable)","user":{"login":"SpicyBadran","id":204524209,"node_id":"U_kgDODDDKsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204524209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran","html_url":"https://github.com/SpicyBadran","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What this is\n\nPhase 2's deliverable for the M18 synthetic-package acceptance item: **a design assessment, on purpose, with no code.** The task's own stop condition applies — *\"if not safely separable: stop at a design assessment; no superficial test for the sake of progress\"* — and this branch records the measurement behind that call so nobody has to re-derive it.\n\nOne file: `evidence/m18-synthetic-package-v1/M18-SYNTHETIC-ACCEPTANCE-DESIGN-ASSESSMENT-20261122.md`. `git diff --name-only 52f682c HEAD` lists only that directory. No roadmap edit, no `notes` added (nothing landed), no milestone state touched.\n\n## The wording, from the authoritative object\n\n`docs/architecture/roadmap.json` @ `52f682c8`, M18: `state=blocked`, `kind=ps5-compatibility`, `level=5`, `depends_on=[M9,M13,M17]` → `in_progress` / `not_started` / `blocked`; `deliverables=[\"platform model loader\"]`; `evidence=[]`; three acceptance items; blocker \"requires a lawful, authenticated input (the M9 payload is absent from the tree) and the trust analysis of M17; PC5 will not decrypt or circumvent\". Only item 3 names a PC5-built input — and all three share one subject, **the loader**:\n\n> \"the load path is exercised against a synthetic package PC5 builds itself, so the mechanism is testable without Sony bytes\"\n\n## Why it is separable in principle, and not yet in practice\n\nSeparable in principle, and the repository already sanctions it: `docs/PS5_SYSTEM_SOFTWARE_TARGET.md` §6 item 4 (`:179–180`) lists exactly this loader against exactly such a package under \"what PC5 can build before any of that is resolved\", and `docs/playstation/SECURITY_BOUNDARY.md:440–441` (on #37's branch) calls the synthetic half \"buildable now and should not wait\".\n\nNot safely separable as an implementation on `main`, for four measured reasons:\n\n| | Blocker | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| B1 | There is no loader — M18's deliverable **is** it | `ls psm/` → 15 files, none a loader/package/pup; `boot/loader.S` is PC5's x86 boot loader, a different subsystem sharing a word |\n| B2 | The execution seam is withheld until M11 | `psm/cpu.py:108` + `psm/conformance.py:114` (`execute_payload` → `UNSUPPORTED`), `psm/registry.py:151` \"(UNSUPPORTED until M11)\"; `M11.state = not_started` |\n| B3 | Nothing to load *from* inside the model | `psm/storage.py:71–87`: `decompress` and `guest_layout` both `unsupported=True` (\"the layout is UNKNOWN and is M21 work\"); `M13.state = not_started` |\n| B4 | The format would have to be invented, and must not imitate authentication | `docs/FIRMWARE_ANALYSIS.md` §7.2 rule 4 forbids decoding an unconfirmed entry table; `C-SEC-01` is RESTRICTED \"not modelled — no PSM interface exists for security state\"; `PS5_PLATFORM_CONTRACT.md:839–843` says M18–M21 consume the contract only through the chain |\n\nSo: separable from the **lawful-input** half (the input can be PC5's own), not separable from **M11 and M13**, which are what give \"load\" a meaning inside the model. A test written today would parse a format invented for the occasion against a loader that does not exist — theatre, not progress.\n\n## Also recorded\n\n* What a synthetic test **could** establish (determinism, the refusal vocabulary `denied` vs `unsupported`, and rejection without writing outside the workspace) and **could not** (the load path, anything about authentication, or M18's completion — `tests/test_product_identity.py:276–283` bars any milestone above level 2 from `complete`, and level 5's `evidence_class` excludes a simulated environment).\n* Existing formats measured rather than duplicated: `tools/firmware.py` is identification-only by policy; `tools/mkiso.py`/`tools/verify_iso.py` carry `PC5BOOT1`/`PC5K`, which is PC5's *disc* contract and not M18's load path; `tests/mbr_fixture.py` and `tests/test_tools.py` are the synthetic-fixture precedent to build on.\n* §6: the design to implement when B1–B3 clear — where the fixture lives, the eight negative controls (truncation at each boundary, bad magic/version, inconsistent lengths and offsets, overflow and unreasonable allocation, missing/duplicate/contradictory metadata, tampered payload and metadata, trailing bytes, unsupported features), the no-writes assertion, the `PC5 synthetic / test-only` labelling rules, and SHA-256 as the ceiling on any integrity field.\n\n## Gates\n\n`TMPDIR=/tmp make docs-check` → **exit 0**, `DOCS OK: 68 Markdown files, 34 make targets`. `TMPDIR=/tmp make check` → **exit 0**: `Ran 929 tests in 61.838s`, `OK (skipped=109)`, `PASSED: 165 checks, 0 failures`, `CITATIONS OK: 258 … across 11 documents`, `PRESENTATION OK: … 13 status rows match roadmap.json`. The test count is **identical to `main`** at `52f682c8`, which is the point: this branch adds a document and no test. Repository gates in this sandbox — not CI (this repository reports no checks), not approval, not evidence about PS5 hardware or Sony's system software.\n\n## Not done here\n\nNo production change, no new interface, no format file, no roadmap edit. M17 and M18 stay `blocked`; M19–M21, M9 and M10 untouched; no acceptance criterion weakened or reworded. Nothing merged.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-22T02:19:34Z","updated_at":"2026-11-22T02:19:34Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"1fd66db6ed45fb970a5dce849ab54bcca2578e65","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"SpicyBadran:feat/m18-synthetic-package","ref":"feat/m18-synthetic-package","repo":{"id":1455102023,"node_id":"R_kgDOVrsYRw","name":"PC5","full_name":"SpicyBadran/PC5","owner":{"login":"SpicyBadran","id":204524209,"node_id":"U_kgDODDDKsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204524209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran","html_url":"https://github.com/SpicyBadran","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/following{/other_user}"